GenCheck
===========================

Usage Instructions:

C:\Program Files (x86)\McKSupport\Tools>GenCheck.exe /?

Program:   GenCheck
Purpose:   Scans iGens, qGens, eGens
Version:   3.0.14 (2022-08-26)
Author:    Scott Allard

Usage: gencheck [[[-m] host1 [etc.]] | [-mx host1 [etc.]]] [-l logCount] [-p phiCount] [-np | -ap]
                [[-srv host1 [etc.]] | [-ex host1 [etc.]]] [-src source1 [etc.]] [-s searchTerm [etc.]]
                [-af arcFilter1 [etc.]] [-e] [-i] [-q] [-a] [-g] [-ms] [-nt TimeStatement] [-ot TimeStatement]

where -m indicates the DICOM source hostnames against which to search and display
         Note: wildcards are supported in source hostNames
         Note: if applied as first arguments, -m is not required for DICOM Source HostNames
where -mx indicates a list of DICOM source hostname in which to exclude the search for (opposite of -m)
         Note: wildcards are NOT supported in source hostNames

where -l indicates the number of iGens/qGens/eGens to dump per DICOM source
where -p indicates the number of iGens/qGens/eGens for which to search for and display PHI (default=1)

where -ap indicates to display PHI for all iGens/qGens/eGens
where -np indicates not to display any PHI for any iGens/qGens/eGens

where -srv indicates a list of server in which to search for phi (default=all)
where -ex indicates a list of server in which to exclude the search for phi (opposite of -srv)
where -src indicates to limit the output to the files that have 'setSourceName' specified in this list (default=all)
where -s indicates to search igen/qgen/egen for the provided search terms
where -af indicates a list of archive controllers (DICOM) to limit the search to

where -e indicates to filter down to show eGens (default=all)
where -i indicates to filter down to show iGens (default=all)
where -q indicates to filter down to show qGens (default=all)
where -a indicates to put all igens into one pool instead of breaking them down by host
where -g indicates to also include logs in staging/Importer folder to search
where -ms indicates to show a summary of modality hosts affected since the time stated by '-nt'
         Note: cannot be used with '-a'

where -nt TimeStatement indicates to only include iGens/qGens/eGens with last modified time newer than TimeStatement
where -ot TimeStatement indicates to only include iGens/qGens/eGens with last modified time older than TimeStatement

Note: TimeStatements can be formatted as "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MI:SS", "Now", or
        "X <second[s] | minute[s] | hour[s] | day[s] | week[s] | month[s] | year[s]> <ago | from now>"

      Please remember to wrap double quotes around statements with spaces!!
      ---------------------------------------------------------------------

